            <ArticleTitle>Nerve entrapment syndromes in the upper limb.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>94-5, 97-8, 100-1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Nerve entrapment in the upper limb usually presents as pain, sensory disturbance and motor loss; the most common diagnosis is carpal tunnel syndrome. A high index of suspicion with some anatomical knowledge aid the recognition of clinical patterns and diagnosis. Treatment of patients with intermittent or early progressive changes has an excellent prognosis; most with constant sensory or motor loss will show at least partial response to treatment.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
